        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Amsterdam</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">1275 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">The settlement grew at the mouth of the Amstel after the flood of 1170, and a dam there is estimated to date from between 1264 and 1275. It is first named in a document of 27 October 1275, which gave its residents an exemption from tolls.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">At the mouth of the Amstel river, where it meets the IJ, in the province of North Holland in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, about 2 metres below sea level.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">The dam in the Amstel and the toll privilege of 1275; herring and the Baltic grain trade; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-golden-age">Dutch Golden Age</a> of the 17th century; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> and its stock exchange; the canal ring; religious refuge for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huguenots">Huguenots</a> and others; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rembrandt">Rembrandt</a>; the occupation of 1940 to 1945 and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deportation">deportation</a> of its Jews</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Amsterdam is the capital and largest city of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, though the government and parliament sit in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-hague">The Hague</a>.</span></div>
